# Comprehensive Synthesis: NHS Winter Pressure Improvement Priorities & Evidence-Based Interventions

---

## SECTION A: CONSOLIDATED PRIORITY MAP

To establish a manuscript-ready foundation for healthcare improvement during winter pressures, candidate priorities generated across the seven stakeholder personas have been synthesised. Overlapping concepts have been merged, terminology normalized, and problems strictly differentiated from interventions. 

### Terminology Normalization Dictionary
* **"Bed-blocking" / "Social delays"** $\rightarrow$ **Delayed Transfers of Care (DTOC) / Criteria to Reside Breaches** managed via **Discharge to Assess (D2A)**.
* **"Hospital at Home" / "Remote monitoring"** $\rightarrow$ **Acute Virtual Wards (AVWs) & Tech-Enabled Remote Patient Monitoring (RPM)**.
* **"Pharmacy First" / "Minor ailment schemes"** $\rightarrow$ **Community Pharmacy Clinical Services (CPCS)**.
* **"Front-door streaming" / "A&E diversion"** $\rightarrow$ **Same Day Emergency Care (SDEC) & Senior-Led Front-Door Triage**.
* **"Cold-sites" / "Surgical hubs"** $\rightarrow$ **Protected Elective Surgical Hubs & Standalone Community Diagnostic Centres (CDCs)**.
* **"Warm home prescriptions" / "Fuel poverty support"** $\rightarrow$ **Targeted Environmental & Energy Subsidies for Vulnerable Respiratory/Cardiovascular Cohorts**.

